  "step_3": "The decision reason requires consideration of the sum of pairwise differences of outcomes between the lotteries. In this case, the only non-zero outcome difference is between -4000 and -3000, which is 1000 in absolute value. The sum of outcome differences is 1000, and it is the same regardless of which lottery is chosen — thus, the reason would be indifferent. However, the individual in the report does not mention outcome differences at all. Instead, they focus solely on the probability difference (20% vs. 25%) and the associated risk of a larger loss. There is no reference to summing outcome differences or evaluating them as a basis for preference. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason. The reported reasoning is based on probability and risk perception, not on outcome differences. The comparisons in the report are about probability, not outcomes. Hence, the decision reason was not used.",
